# TASK-260728-3a2dnr — results

Replan of the board, specs, and execution graph against the owner-approved macOS
prototype strategy. 2026-07-28. No tunnel product code was written; `Sources`,
`Tests`, `Protocol`, `relay`, `scripts`, `config`, `Package.swift`, and
`Makefile` are untouched.

## 1. Canonical artifacts updated (AC1)

| File | Change |
| --- | --- |
| `.spec/decisions.md` | ADR-013 re-scoped to a **release-path** gate (A0 is not a prototype gate). ADR-014 moved Open → **Accepted: libssh2 primary**, NIOSSH retained as comparative evidence. New **ADR-023** (M0 SSH viability scope, Option A, with the four deferred semantics named and owned). New **ADR-024** (macOS-only physical target, iOS deferred, Linux CI nonblocking, Relux Works signing/notary availability, Keychain-only secrets). Rationale section explains why narrowing *when* evidence is owed does not weaken *whether*. |
| `.spec/ssh-transport.md` | Engine gate table split into **Tier 1 — M0-viability-mandatory** (10 rows, all binding) and **Tier 2 — M3 evidence-gated** (the four deferred semantics, each with the pinned-source reason and owner task `TASK-260728-3cveay`). Adapters must surface Tier-2 items as explicit not-reported/unsupported states; fabricating a value fails the adapter. |
| `.spec/validation.md` | Architecture-gate table gains a **Path** column: A0 = release path only; P0 = macOS-only on this Mac; M0 SSH = Tier-1 rows; M5 App Store split out and deferred with iOS. Principles updated: physical hardware means this Apple-silicon Mac; iPhone/jetsam rows are named deferred gaps, never passes. |
| `.spec/delivery.md` | M0 exit now excludes A0 and requires every deferred SSH semantic to have a named M3 owner. M1 exit is macOS-only. Critical-dependency chain rewritten to start at Ceremony C1 and to place A0 → iOS → M5 on a deferred branch. |
| `.spec/goal-macos-v1.md` | Rewritten. New **Approved strategy (binding)** section encodes all six owner decisions. Stop-the-line section replaced: **Ceremony C1** as the single up-front human permission session, then ordered later gates. Invariants section gains an explicit clause that M0 viability scoping relaxes nothing. |

