scope:In scope: consumer-driven receive-window credit with an immutable per-channel cap that is not auto-adjusted before consumer delivery; RFC 4254 channel-open rejection reason taxonomy preserved end to end; exact exec-exit metadata distinguishing status 0 from absent metadata and exposing exit-signal coreDumped; deep rekey and keepalive observability including server-initiated KEX lifecycle/generation and reply-correlated keepalive RTT, timeout, and miss metrics; the fork or upstream change needed on the selected engine plus its maintenance and rebase owner; conformance tests and harness evidence. Out of scope: re-opening the M0 engine selection, NIOSSH fork work while libssh2 remains primary, lane scheduling policy, and hardcoding numeric window or rekey values outside the accepted memory ledger.
